    "summary": "Created a standalone Java PoV that drives the real production sink org.ff4j.utils.MappingUtil#instanceFlippingStrategy with an attacker-controlled class name that does not implement FlippingStrategy. The class's no-arg constructor executes as an observable side effect before the post-construction cast fails, proving the sink performs Class.forName(...).newInstance() with no base-type check. This is the shared root-cause pattern (unchecked reflective construction from an attacker string) that recurs across every trace in the alert: PropertiesParser flip-strategy/property-type parsing, XmlParser property-type and flip-strategy parsing, PropertyFactory.createProperty, FeatureJsonParser/PropertyJsonParser via MappingUtil, and the embedded web console's ConsoleOperations.createFeature."
