    "patch_notes": "Root cause: multiple call sites did Class.forName(attackerString).newInstance() (or Constructor(String,String).newInstance()) and only checked the expected base type via an implicit cast AFTER construction, so the attacker's constructor (and any side effects: file writes, network calls, JNDI, static initializers) had already executed by the time the ClassCastException surfaced and was swallowed.\n\nFix: added MappingUtil.loadClass(String className, Class<T> expectedType) which does Class.forName/classLoader.loadClass, then checks expectedType.isAssignableFrom(rawClazz) and throws IllegalArgumentException immediately if not assignable \u2014 no instance is ever created for a class outside the expected type. This is now the single choke point used at every flip-strategy sink (MappingUtil.instanceFlippingStrategy, XmlParser.parseFlipStrategy, PropertiesParser.parseFeatures, YamlParser.parseFlipStrategy, ConsoleOperations.createFeature/updateFlippingStrategy) with expectedType=FlippingStrategy.class, and inside PropertyFactory.createProperty(String,String,String,String,Set) with expectedType=Property.class for property-type construction (which XmlParser, PropertiesParser and YamlParser's property-type parsing now delegate to instead of duplicating their own Class.forName+getConstructor logic).\n\nOut of scope / intentionally not touched: ConsoleServlet.init / FF4jServlet.init load an FF4jProvider class from a servlet init-param (deployment-time trust boundary, configured by the application owner via web.xml, not runtime attacker input) \u2014 different threat model from the alert's traces. PropertyClass.fromString does Class.forName(v) but never calls newInstance() \u2014 it stores the resolved Class object itself as the property's value by design, not a construction sink, so it is not CWE-094.\n\nRemoved now-unreachable `catch (ClassNotFoundException e)` clauses in ConsoleOperations where Class.forName was replaced by MappingUtil.loadClass (which throws unchecked IllegalArgumentException instead), and dropped now-unused `java.lang.reflect.Constructor` imports from XmlParser, PropertiesParser and YamlParser after delegating to PropertyFactory.",
